{%- comment -%}
  App Embed Block — target: head. ONE block that owns the whole feature:
  pre-paint FOUC prevention, JSON data island, controller script and the
  custom-element placeholder. Shopify injects this just before </head>,
  so the inline <style>/<script>/<link>/JSON-island parts are parsed
  during <head> parsing — before the <body> / native gallery is painted,
  which is the only true pre-paint hook.

  How the HTML parser places things:
    Everything except <cp-embed-gallery> is head-valid (<style>, <script>,
    <link>) and stays in <head>. The <cp-embed-gallery> placeholder is
    NOT head-valid, so when the parser encounters it the head insertion
    mode ends implicitly (per HTML5 spec) and the element is placed as
    the FIRST <body> child. The deferred controller script (registered
    in head) then upgrades that placeholder and `connectedCallback`
    fires → _init resolves the native gallery, hides it per-element,
    releases the blanket class and mounts the custom gallery.

  FOUC flow:
    1. Setter script (synchronous, head-parse) reads the JSON data island
       above it and, ONLY if the current variant actually has images
       (resolved from ?variant= or product.selected_or_first_available_
       variant — [name="id"] does not exist yet at head-parse), adds
       `cp-vg-prehide` to <html>. The blanket <style> hides all default-
       selector native galleries pre-paint via visibility:hidden (layout
       reserved → no shift when revealed).
    2. window.__cpVgFouc.prehideTimer (3s) is the only fail-safe to drop
       the class if the controller never mounts.
    3. The deferred controller runs at DOMContentLoaded, _tick releases
       the blanket synchronously THEN applies the precise per-element
       .cp-vg-native-hidden hide in the same tick → no flash. On AJAX
       variant switch the controller re-adds the blanket synchronously
       (observer + event handlers gated by _needsCover) and releases on
       the next tick.

  Constraints (Shopify): app embed blocks have only Global Liquid scope
  (`product` is available on product pages). The bundled Shopify
  stylesheet tag is forbidden in app blocks — plain <style>/<script>
  only. Custom elements as direct head children are not head-valid, so
  the placeholder MUST be last in this block (or the parser closes head
  early and metadata after it ends up in body).
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if product != blank -%}

{%- comment -%}
  R3-H1: `| json` escapes JSON syntax but NOT `<`, so an attacker-influenced
  variant.title containing `</script><script>…` would break out of this
  JSON island and inject script regardless of the JS-side _esc(). Every
  free-text value interpolated into the island MUST additionally neutralise
  `<`/`>` by replacing them with their \uXXXX JSON escapes (JSON.parse
  restores them, so data is unchanged). That now happens in ONE place:
  snippets/cp-vg-item prints each object with both characters escaped, so
  every string in it (alt text, URLs, ids) is covered.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Fallback memo (variants without any gallery metafield). The fallback emits
  every product.media for EACH such variant, and a `render` per entry per
  variant would be thousands of renders on a product with many variants. So
  every product.media is rendered once, and only when the first variant needs
  it (cp_fb_built): the item's media id, `<`, its JSON object, `>`. `<` and
  `>` are safe separators because cp-vg-item's output never contains either
  (it escapes both inside strings). It is ONE capture over product.media (a per-media
  append would copy the growing memo every time), split once into cp_fb_items;
  cp_fb_items stays nil for a product whose
  variants all have metafields.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign cp_fb_items = nil -%}
{%- assign cp_fb_built = false -%}
<script type="application/json" id="cp-embed-data-{{ block.id }}">
  {
    {%- for variant in product.variants -%}
      {%- assign vg = variant.metafields.custom.variant_gallery -%}
      {%- assign cp_order_mf = variant.metafields.custom.variant_gallery_order -%}
      {%- assign cp_models_mf = variant.metafields.custom.variant_3d_models -%}
      {%- assign cp_previews_mf = variant.metafields.custom.variant_3d_previews -%}
      "{{ variant.id }}": [
        {%- assign cp_has_any = false -%}
        {%- assign cp_seen_file_ids = ',' -%}
        {%- assign cp_seen_urls = ',' -%}
        {%- assign cp_seen_models = ',' -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Precomputed booleans for the if/elsif chain below. Liquid does
          not support parenthesised boolean expressions like
          `(a and b) or (c and d)`, so the sub-conditions are flattened
          here into named flags that the chain can OR together.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign cp_has_vg     = false -%}
        {%- assign cp_has_models = false -%}
        {%- if vg != blank and vg.value != blank -%}{%- assign cp_has_vg = true -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- if cp_models_mf != blank and cp_models_mf.value != blank -%}{%- assign cp_has_models = true -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Every entry below is ONE render of snippets/cp-vg-item, always in
          these two lines. The snippet prints a JSON object or nothing.
          Shopify wraps a snippet's output in "<!-- BEGIN app snippet -->"
          comments that `capture` keeps, so the second line cuts them off
          while printing (cp-external-video documents why) and tests for an
          object with `contains '"type"'` (every object has that key, the
          annotation never does) instead of assigning the cut value first:
          every assign counts against Shopify's memory limit. The comma and
          cp_has_any stay HERE because `render` is scope-isolated.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Voll-mix path: variant_gallery_order (json) is a unified array of
          { kind: 'file' | 'url' | 'model', value } entries that mirrors how
          the merchant drag-arranged files + external URLs + 3D models in
          the admin. When present we iterate it as the primary source of
          order, then append unreferenced items (new uploads / URLs / models
          added since the last save).
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if cp_order_mf != blank and cp_order_mf.value != blank -%}
          {%- if variant.featured_image != blank -%}
            {%- assign vfi = variant.featured_image -%}
            {%- assign vfi_id_str = vfi.id | append: '' -%}
            {%- assign cp_seen_file_ids = cp_seen_file_ids | append: vfi_id_str | append: ',' -%}
            {%- capture cp_o -%}{%- render 'cp-vg-item', m: vfi, kind: 'image', fb: variant.title -%}{%- endcapture -%}
            {%- if cp_o contains '"type"' -%}{%- if cp_has_any %},{% endif -%}{{ cp_o | split: '-->' | last | split: '<!--' | first | strip }}{%- assign cp_has_any = true -%}{%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- for entry in cp_order_mf.value -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              The branches below only PICK what to emit: cp_rm (a vg.value
              item), cp_ru (an external URL) or cp_rmod + cp_rpv (a model URL
              and its preview); `continue` skips the entry (dedup). One render
              at the end of the iteration. Reset first, before any continue.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- assign cp_rm = nil -%}
            {%- assign cp_ru = nil -%}
            {%- assign cp_rmod = nil -%}
            {%- assign cp_rpv = nil -%}
            {%- assign entry_val = entry.value | append: '' -%}
            {%- if entry.kind == 'file' -%}
              {%- assign needle = ',' | append: entry_val | append: ',' -%}
              {%- if cp_seen_file_ids contains needle -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- for item in vg.value -%}
                {%- assign item_id_str = item.id | append: '' -%}
                {%- if item_id_str == entry_val -%}
                  {%- assign cp_seen_file_ids = cp_seen_file_ids | append: entry_val | append: ',' -%}
                  {%- if item.media_type == 'image' or item.media_type == 'video' -%}{%- assign cp_rm = item -%}{%- endif -%}
                  {%- break -%}
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            {%- elsif entry.kind == 'url' -%}
              {%- comment -%} url_encode removes the comma (and other special chars), so the comma-joined cp_seen_urls set's `,VALUE,` substring check stays safe for URLs that legitimately contain commas (e.g. Vimeo privacy hash, ?list=a,b,c). {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- assign url_token = entry_val | url_encode -%}
              {%- assign url_needle = ',' | append: url_token | append: ',' -%}
              {%- if cp_seen_urls contains url_needle -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- assign cp_seen_urls = cp_seen_urls | append: url_token | append: ',' -%}
              {%- assign cp_ru = entry_val | strip -%}
            {%- elsif entry.kind == 'model' -%}
              {%- comment -%} Same comma-safe membership pattern as the url branch. {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- assign model_token = entry_val | url_encode -%}
              {%- assign model_needle = ',' | append: model_token | append: ',' -%}
              {%- if cp_seen_models contains model_needle -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- assign cp_seen_models = cp_seen_models | append: model_token | append: ',' -%}
              {%- assign cp_rmod = entry_val | strip -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                Look up the parallel JPEG preview (custom.variant_3d_previews
                is a list.url metafield aligned 1:1 with variant_3d_models by
                index). voll-mix path has no natural index — the entry came
                from the order JSON — so we re-scan cp_models_mf.value to
                find this URL's position, then pull the same-index preview.
                Empty string when the metafield is missing or the slot has
                no preview yet (legacy models from before this metafield).
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- if cp_previews_mf != blank and cp_previews_mf.value != blank and cp_models_mf != blank and cp_models_mf.value != blank -%}
                {%- for cp_m_url in cp_models_mf.value -%}
                  {%- if cp_m_url == cp_rmod -%}
                    {%- assign cp_rpv = cp_previews_mf.value[forloop.index0] | default: '' -%}
                    {%- break -%}
                  {%- endif -%}
                {%- endfor -%}
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- capture cp_o -%}{%- render 'cp-vg-item', m: cp_rm, url: cp_ru, model: cp_rmod, preview: cp_rpv, alt: cp_rm.alt, fb: variant.title -%}{%- endcapture -%}
            {%- if cp_o contains '"type"' -%}{%- if cp_has_any %},{% endif -%}{{ cp_o | split: '-->' | last | split: '<!--' | first | strip }}{%- assign cp_has_any = true -%}{%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            Tail-emit: any vg.value items whose id is missing from the order
            metafield (e.g. files added after the last reorder save) are
            appended in their natural vg.value order, so they're still
            visible on the storefront.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if vg != blank and vg.value != blank -%}
            {%- for item in vg.value -%}
              {%- assign item_id_str = item.id | append: '' -%}
              {%- assign tail_needle = ',' | append: item_id_str | append: ',' -%}
              {%- if cp_seen_file_ids contains tail_needle -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- assign cp_seen_file_ids = cp_seen_file_ids | append: item_id_str | append: ',' -%}
              {%- if item.media_type == 'image' or item.media_type == 'video' -%}
                {%- capture cp_o -%}{%- render 'cp-vg-item', m: item, alt: item.alt, fb: variant.title -%}{%- endcapture -%}
                {%- if cp_o contains '"type"' -%}{%- if cp_has_any %},{% endif -%}{{ cp_o | split: '-->' | last | split: '<!--' | first | strip }}{%- assign cp_has_any = true -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- assign cp_tail_extvids = variant.metafields.custom.variant_external_videos -%}
          {%- if cp_tail_extvids != blank and cp_tail_extvids.value != blank -%}
            {%- for cp_url_raw in cp_tail_extvids.value -%}
              {%- assign cp_url = cp_url_raw | strip -%}
              {%- assign url_tail_token = cp_url | url_encode -%}
              {%- assign url_tail_needle = ',' | append: url_tail_token | append: ',' -%}
              {%- if cp_seen_urls contains url_tail_needle -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- assign cp_seen_urls = cp_seen_urls | append: url_tail_token | append: ',' -%}
              {%- capture cp_o -%}{%- render 'cp-vg-item', url: cp_url, fb: variant.title -%}{%- endcapture -%}
              {%- if cp_o contains '"type"' -%}{%- if cp_has_any %},{% endif -%}{{ cp_o | split: '-->' | last | split: '<!--' | first | strip }}{%- assign cp_has_any = true -%}{%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            Tail-emit for 3D models added since the last reorder save:
            handleAddThreeDModelUrl in the admin only writes
            variant_3d_models, NOT variant_gallery_order. Without this
            loop, a model added to a variant with an existing order JSON
            would be visible in the admin (the orderedUrls memo appends
            unseen URLs) but invisible on the storefront — silent state
            drift between admin and storefront. The dedup against
            cp_seen_models ensures models that ARE already in the order
            JSON aren't double-emitted.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if cp_models_mf != blank and cp_models_mf.value != blank -%}
            {%- for cp_model_url_raw in cp_models_mf.value -%}
              {%- assign cp_model_url = cp_model_url_raw | strip -%}
              {%- assign model_tail_token = cp_model_url | url_encode -%}
              {%- assign model_tail_needle = ',' | append: model_tail_token | append: ',' -%}
              {%- if cp_seen_models contains model_tail_needle -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- assign cp_seen_models = cp_seen_models | append: model_tail_token | append: ',' -%}
              {%- comment -%} Parallel preview lookup by index — forloop.index0 maps directly to the same slot in custom.variant_3d_previews. {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- assign cp_model_preview = '' -%}
              {%- if cp_previews_mf != blank and cp_previews_mf.value != blank -%}
                {%- assign cp_model_preview = cp_previews_mf.value[forloop.index0] | default: '' -%}
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- capture cp_o -%}{%- render 'cp-vg-item', model: cp_model_url, preview: cp_model_preview, fb: variant.title -%}{%- endcapture -%}
              {%- if cp_o contains '"type"' -%}{%- if cp_has_any %},{% endif -%}{{ cp_o | split: '-->' | last | split: '<!--' | first | strip }}{%- assign cp_has_any = true -%}{%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Default path (no variant_gallery_order yet): existing behaviour —
          featured_image, then vg.value items, then external URLs, then
          3D models. The branch also fires when ONLY models are set so a
          variant with just a .glb is not silently dropped into the
          product.media fallback.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- elsif cp_has_vg or cp_has_models -%}
          {%- if variant.featured_image != blank -%}
            {%- capture cp_o -%}{%- render 'cp-vg-item', m: variant.featured_image, kind: 'image', fb: variant.title -%}{%- endcapture -%}
            {%- if cp_o contains '"type"' -%}{%- if cp_has_any %},{% endif -%}{{ cp_o | split: '-->' | last | split: '<!--' | first | strip }}{%- assign cp_has_any = true -%}{%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            Default order (when variant_gallery_order is not set):
            ALL images first (vg.value natural order, preceded by featured_image
            above), then ALL native videos, then external videos, then 3D models.
            We split vg.value into two passes — pass 1 emits image entries only,
            pass 2 emits video entries only — so a video inserted between two
            images in the metafield does not break up the image group on the
            storefront. The merchant-defined mix order is still respected via
            the voll-mix path above when variant_gallery_order IS set.
            No vg-model branch here either: Shopify `list.file_reference`
            returns MediaImage / Video / GenericFile only — variant-specific
            3D models live in custom.variant_3d_models (list.url) and are
            emitted after the external-video loop.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- for item in vg.value -%}
            {%- if item.media_type == 'image' -%}
              {%- capture cp_o -%}{%- render 'cp-vg-item', m: item, alt: item.alt, fb: variant.title -%}{%- endcapture -%}
              {%- if cp_o contains '"type"' -%}{%- if cp_has_any %},{% endif -%}{{ cp_o | split: '-->' | last | split: '<!--' | first | strip }}{%- assign cp_has_any = true -%}{%- endif -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
          {%- for item in vg.value -%}
            {%- if item.media_type == 'video' -%}
              {%- capture cp_o -%}{%- render 'cp-vg-item', m: item, alt: item.alt, fb: variant.title -%}{%- endcapture -%}
              {%- if cp_o contains '"type"' -%}{%- if cp_has_any %},{% endif -%}{{ cp_o | split: '-->' | last | split: '<!--' | first | strip }}{%- assign cp_has_any = true -%}{%- endif -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            YouTube/Vimeo URLs from custom.variant_external_videos (list.url).
            `list.file_reference` can't hold URLs, so they live on a parallel
            metafield and are appended after the file-backed items. URL parsing
            happens in snippets/cp-external-video (called by cp-vg-item). The
            controller's existing `external_video` dispatch handles these
            unchanged — only host + external_id are required at runtime.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- assign cp_extvids = variant.metafields.custom.variant_external_videos -%}
          {%- if cp_extvids != blank and cp_extvids.value != blank -%}
            {%- for cp_url_raw in cp_extvids.value -%}
              {%- assign cp_url = cp_url_raw | strip -%}
              {%- capture cp_o -%}{%- render 'cp-vg-item', url: cp_url, fb: variant.title -%}{%- endcapture -%}
              {%- if cp_o contains '"type"' -%}{%- if cp_has_any %},{% endif -%}{{ cp_o | split: '-->' | last | split: '<!--' | first | strip }}{%- assign cp_has_any = true -%}{%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            3D models from custom.variant_3d_models (list.url). Shopify's
            list.file_reference rejects Media3d, so variant-scoped models
            live in this parallel list.url metafield. .glb URLs are emitted
            directly; <model-viewer> on the storefront knows how to handle
            them without a Shopify-side preview image.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if cp_models_mf != blank and cp_models_mf.value != blank -%}
            {%- for cp_model_url_raw in cp_models_mf.value -%}
              {%- assign cp_model_url = cp_model_url_raw | strip -%}
              {%- comment -%} Parallel preview lookup — same index in variant_3d_previews. {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- assign cp_model_preview = '' -%}
              {%- if cp_previews_mf != blank and cp_previews_mf.value != blank -%}
                {%- assign cp_model_preview = cp_previews_mf.value[forloop.index0] | default: '' -%}
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- capture cp_o -%}{%- render 'cp-vg-item', model: cp_model_url, preview: cp_model_preview, fb: variant.title -%}{%- endcapture -%}
              {%- if cp_o contains '"type"' -%}{%- if cp_has_any %},{% endif -%}{{ cp_o | split: '-->' | last | split: '<!--' | first | strip }}{%- assign cp_has_any = true -%}{%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- comment -%} Step 2: if no images from metafield, fall back to product.media. Handles ALL media types so a merchant-uploaded video / 3D model is no longer silently dropped (Bilder + Video-Player). featured_image emitted first as primary (RISK-4) and deduped from the loop. {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- unless cp_has_any -%}
          {%- assign cp_vfi_id = '' -%}
          {%- if variant.featured_image != blank -%}
            {%- capture cp_o -%}{%- render 'cp-vg-item', m: variant.featured_image, kind: 'image', fb: variant.title -%}{%- endcapture -%}
            {%- if cp_o contains '"type"' -%}{%- if cp_has_any %},{% endif -%}{{ cp_o | split: '-->' | last | split: '<!--' | first | strip }}{%- assign cp_has_any = true -%}{%- endif -%}
            {%- assign cp_vfi_id = variant.featured_image.id -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- comment -%} Built lazily, once per product (see the memo comment above the capture). {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- unless cp_fb_built -%}
            {%- assign cp_fb_built = true -%}
            {%- capture cp_fb -%}
              {%- for media in product.media -%}
                {%- capture cp_o -%}{%- render 'cp-vg-item', m: media, alt: media.alt, fb: product.title -%}{%- endcapture -%}
                {%- if cp_o contains '"type"' -%}{{ media.id }}<{{ cp_o | split: '-->' | last | split: '<!--' | first | strip }}>{%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            {%- endcapture -%}
            {%- assign cp_fb_items = cp_fb | split: '>' -%}
          {%- endunless -%}
          {%- comment -%} Ids compare as strings; no featured image is '', which matches no media id (as blank did). {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- assign cp_vfi_key = cp_vfi_id | append: '' -%}
          {%- for cp_fb_item in cp_fb_items -%}
            {%- assign cp_fb_id = cp_fb_item | split: '<' | first -%}
            {%- if cp_fb_id != cp_vfi_key -%}{%- if cp_has_any %},{% endif -%}{{ cp_fb_item | split: '<' | last }}{%- assign cp_has_any = true -%}{%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endunless -%}
      ]{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
    {%- endfor -%}
  }
</script>

{%- comment -%}
  Pre-paint setter. Reads the JSON island above (single source of truth,
  no duplicated has-images logic), resolves the current variant from
  ?variant= or selected_or_first_available_variant (no [name="id"] in
  the DOM yet at head-parse time — the controller handles late
  corrections), and adds `cp-vg-prehide` to <html> ONLY if data[id] is
  non-empty. This is now perfectly aligned with the controller decision
  (a variant whose variant_gallery is set but whose every image_url is
  empty yields an empty data[id] and is NOT pre-hidden).

  Security: only numeric IDs and the canonical class literal are used —
  no merchant-controlled value is interpolated into JS strings here.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script>
  (function () {
    try {
      var el = document.getElementById('cp-embed-data-{{ block.id }}');
      if (!el) return;
      var data = JSON.parse(el.textContent);
      var id = null;
      try { id = new URL(window.location.href).searchParams.get('variant'); } catch (e) {}
      if (!id) id = {{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.id | json }};
      if (id == null) return;
      var imgs = data[String(id)];
      if (!(imgs && imgs.length)) return;
      document.documentElement.classList.add('cp-vg-prehide');
      window.__cpVgFouc = window.__cpVgFouc || {};
      window.__cpVgFouc.prehideTimer = window.setTimeout(function () {
        document.documentElement.classList.remove('cp-vg-prehide');
      }, 3000);
    } catch (e) { /* never block page render */ }
  })();
</script>

{%- comment -%}
  CANONICAL native-selector list. Kept in sync with the _selectors array
  in assets/variant-gallery-embed.js — change both together.
  visibility:hidden reserves layout (no shift when the blanket is
  released and the controller's per-element display:none takes over).
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  html.cp-vg-prehide media-gallery,
  html.cp-vg-prehide [id^="MediaGallery"],
  html.cp-vg-prehide .product__media-wrapper,
  html.cp-vg-prehide .product__media-list { visibility: hidden !important; }
</style>

<style>.cp-vg-native-hidden{display:none !important;}</style>

{{ 'variant-gallery-embed.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
<script src="{{ 'variant-gallery-embed.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

{%- comment -%}
  Placeholder element. NOT head-valid per HTML5, so the parser closes
  <head> implicitly when it reaches this tag and places the element as
  the first <body> child. Everything above (head-valid) therefore stays
  in <head> and is parsed pre-paint. Keep this LAST inside the if-block
  for that invariant to hold.
{%- endcomment -%}
<cp-embed-gallery
  id="cp-embed-gallery-{{ block.id }}"
  class="cp-embed-gallery"
  style="--cp-thumb-size: {{ block.settings.thumbnail_size }}px; display: none;"
  data-block-id="{{ block.id }}"
  data-native-selector="{{ block.settings.native_gallery_selector }}"
  data-scope-selector="{{ block.settings.scope_selector }}"
  data-extra-hide="{{ block.settings.extra_hide_selector }}"
  data-thumb-size="{{ block.settings.thumbnail_size }}"
  data-show-thumbs="{% if block.settings.enable_thumbnails %}1{% endif %}"
  data-thumb-pos="{{ block.settings.thumbnail_position | default: 'bottom' }}"
  data-inherit-theme="{% if block.settings.inherit_theme_settings == false %}0{% else %}1{% endif %}"
  data-model-viewer-src="{{ 'model-viewer.min.js' | asset_url }}"
>
  <div class="cp-gallery__inner"></div>
</cp-embed-gallery>

{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Variant Image Gallery",
  "target": "head",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "inherit_theme_settings",
      "label": "Inherit theme gallery settings (recommended)",
      "default": true,
      "info": "When on, the gallery automatically follows the theme's own product-gallery settings — thumbnail position, layout (stacked vs. with thumbs), mobile thumbnail behaviour, video looping. The settings below are ignored. Turn off only if you want to override the theme."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "enable_thumbnails",
      "label": "Show thumbnails",
      "default": false,
      "info": "Override (ignored when Inherit theme settings is on). Off: all relevant images stack vertically at full width. On: a single main image is shown with a clickable thumbnail strip in the position chosen below."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "thumbnail_position",
      "label": "Thumbnail position",
      "default": "bottom",
      "options": [
        { "value": "bottom", "label": "Below main image" },
        { "value": "top", "label": "Above main image" },
        { "value": "left", "label": "Left of main image" },
        { "value": "right", "label": "Right of main image" }
      ],
      "info": "Only applies when 'Show thumbnails' is enabled. Long lists scroll horizontally (top/bottom) or vertically (left/right) with arrow controls on hover."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "thumbnail_size",
      "label": "Thumbnail size (px)",
      "min": 60,
      "max": 200,
      "step": 10,
      "default": 80
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "native_gallery_selector",
      "label": "Native gallery CSS selector",
      "default": "media-gallery",
      "info": "CSS selector of your theme's native product image gallery. Default works for Dawn theme. For other themes inspect the gallery element and enter its tag or class (e.g. .product__media-wrapper)."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "scope_selector",
      "label": "Product container selector (optional)",
      "info": "Restricts the native gallery search to this container so quick-view / modal galleries elsewhere on the page are not matched. Leave empty for the whole page."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "extra_hide_selector",
      "label": "Extra elements to hide (optional)",
      "info": "Comma-separated CSS selectors for separate native thumbnail / zoom elements some themes render outside the gallery. Leave empty unless leftover native thumbnails appear."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Automatically replaces the native product gallery with variant-specific images from ContentPilot AI. Enable this embed once — no block placement needed."
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
